 $y=5x-2$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T?$" 13194139535131 true] [17592186332844 1113 #uuid "47415e24-3b44-5963-9e4f-d6be1c41588d" 13194139535131 true] [17592186332844 1145 "First, notice that the line $y=5x-2$ passes through the points $A(0,-2)$ and $B(1,3)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $A$ and $B$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -15\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${A}^{′}(0,8)$ and ${B}^{′}(1,-15).$\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${A}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-8 & =\\frac{-15-8}{1-0}(x-0) \\\\ y-8 & =-23x \\\\ 23x+y-8 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535131 true] [17592186332845 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332846 13194139535131 true] [17592186332845 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332847 13194139535131 true] [17592186332845 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332848 13194139535131 true] [17592186332845 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332849 13194139535131 true] [17592186332845 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332850 13194139535131 true] [17592186332845 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535131 true] [17592186332845 1041 "selection" 13194139535131 true] [17592186332845 1104 #edb/ref 17592186332849 13194139535131 true] [17592186332845 1110 #uuid "520b8fd0-01eb-5230-ae3d-37cf2380d512" 13194139535131 true] [1759